SOAPBOX: WPX is always fun, but high indexes "supported by" local snow and sleet made this year a very noisy experience. The use of Artificial and very Un-Intelligent voice keying by operators perfectly able to speak, is not a positive development, including the use of female voices by male operators with no gender incongruence. I much prefer communicating with a real person who is able to understand that I am not responding to his/her call, but a different station on the same frequency, instead of a insistent AI voice keyer only repeating its message. And I'd love to compete and communicate with a human operator, not a computer. I can only hope AUI voice keying is a fad to be soon forgotten.
